Command:        QWK
Purpose:        To upload a QWK message packet
Available at:   Main>

QWK packets are compressed files which contain a number of seperate text messages from a BBS.

Entering QWK from the Main> menu will begin the process of uploading your responses to a previously created/read QWK packet.  Once you enter QWK from Main> you will be asked if you wish to use your default transfer protocol.  Select the protocol you wish to use.  The system will then ask you to begin sending the packet or abort.  Press Return to upload the packet, or A to abort.

Once you have successfully uploaded a QWK packet, the system will then notify you that it is posting your messages/responses, and show the name of each post/response.

Please select YANK for more information on creating/downloading a QWK packet.  Additional help is available on the following Base topics:

DROP            RANGES          SCAN           YANK
